    "knownIssues": ["A formula is not a substance: ethanol and dimethyl ether share C2H6O. The registry is keyed by CAS RN, and the formula must agree with the record.", "Tabulated values differ between sources; each step keeps the alternatives, and the script checks that the state at 25 °C does not depend on which source is used.", "Equations of state extrapolate below the triple point without complaint (CoolProp gives CO2 a 'boiling point' of 185.10 K at 1 atm); the classifier never uses a liquid-vapor curve below the triple point.", "Off 1 atm, vapor and sublimation pressures are interpolated linearly in ln p against 1/T between the triple, normal, and critical points, and melting lines are taken as vertical. Classifications near a phase boundary are approximate; the phase test points measure how approximate."]
  },
